{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically elicited the patient's current episode status, identified critical information gaps, recognized implant-stent and pure red cell aplasia risks, differentiated orders from results, maintained diagnostic boundaries, and built an executable follow‑up plan with teach‑back. All seven responsibility‑chain duties are met without error. Four high‑order points were actively triggered and completed with meaningful trajectory impact: HO1 (repairing the multi‑specialty handoff for antiplatelet/anemia/surgical clearance), HO2 (building a practical records‑recovery workflow despite blurred photos and external‑system gaps), HO3 (delivering a bounded closure with explicit residual‑risk classification and caregiver teach‑back), and HO4 (reconstructing the clinical timeline from contradictory fragments into distinct phases). No important non‑chain defect is present. The trajectory therefore satisfies Grade 5 (Perfect).",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00338",
        "explanation": "Doctor reframes caregiver's understanding of the bounded plan and obtains explicit confirmation that care continues with original antiplatelet regimen while awaiting formal written scheme from thoracic surgery.",
        "quote": "您理解得完全正确：现在只是把心内科会诊流程正式接上了，但还没有正式方案"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00718",
        "explanation": "Doctor delivers a bounded‑episode closure focusing on the four‑item written scheme, residual risks, and red‑flag thresholds, and obtains caregiver confirmation.",
        "quote": "闭 episode 的安全边界：只要没有由胸外科牵头、联合心内科和麻醉科共同出具的、包含四项核心内容的书面方案，就绝不能视为可以执行的安排"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The trajectory closes with a concrete, caregiver‑confirmed next‑step plan: continue current antiplatelet medication, discard the old preoperative checklist, complete the scheduled CT in 4–6 weeks, and demand a four‑item written perioperative plan from thoracic surgery. Residual risks (nodule size/features, exact antiplatelet adjustment, pathology) are explicitly carried forward with a named owner and time window, and red‑flag symptoms are clearly linked to emergency escalation.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00718",
        "explanation": "Doctor defines the four‑item written scheme that must be obtained from thoracic surgery before any perioperative medication change, thereby assigning each unresolved risk to a responsible service channel and keeping safety boundaries intact.",
        "quote": "包含四项核心内容的书面方案：\n1. 支架药是否需要停？何时停？是否需要桥接？用什么药物？\n2. 手术时间是否已确定？最晚何时通知？\n3. 若未按时通知，应拨打哪个电话、去哪个窗口跟进？\n4. 负责医生或联系人的姓名"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00338",
        "explanation": "Doctor correctly interprets the procedural step (cardiology consultation initiated but no formal plan) and translates it into a safe interim action: continue original antiplatelet therapy while waiting for written confirmation.",
        "quote": "只是把心内科会诊流程正式接上了，但还没有正式方案，手术安排和用药调整都必须等心内科出具书面意见后才能确定"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_01021",
        "explanation": "Doctor integrates previously collected evidence (old preoperative form, medication bag, nurse station note) to drive a unified, persistent demand for a written perioperative plan.",
        "quote": "您看到的“病例已转入联合术前复核流程”和“原术前准备单暂停执行”确实不是手术取消"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00032",
        "explanation": "Doctor immediately flags the critical risk of self‑discontinuing antiplatelet medication after coronary stenting, emphasizing that it can cause stent thrombosis, myocardial infarction, or sudden death.",
        "quote": "支架术后抗血小板药物（如阿司匹林、氯吡格雷）绝对不能自行停用，否则可能引发支架内血栓，危及生命"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00272",
        "explanation": "Doctor advises the caregiver to write a reminder note and place it on the medication bag to prevent the patient from mistakenly following the old preoperative order.",
        "quote": "把“等胸外科正式电话，不能自己停药”这句话写在便签上贴在药袋旁"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "excellent",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "excellent",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "excellent",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "excellent",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "excellent"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00718",
          "explanation": "Doctor assigns each unresolved risk (antiplatelet medication, operative clearance, anemia severity) to the correct responsible service—thoracic surgery, cardiology, hematology—and specifies the questions the caregiver must ask each service, thereby repairing the broken responsibility chain.",
          "quote": "必须由胸外科牵头，联合心内科、麻醉科、血液科共同出具包含以下四项内容的正式书面方案"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00960",
          "explanation": "Doctor further specifies that if thoracic surgery still fails to provide a written plan, the caregiver should escalate to cardiology and anesthesiology joint evaluation, keeping interim safety boundaries intact.",
          "quote": "立即转诊至心内科和麻醉科联合门诊评估，由两个专科共同出具“是否可安全手术”及“围术期用药管理”的书面意见"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO1 is triggered when the caregiver cannot name stent medications, lacks recent blood counts, and only knows that ‘doctors looked at it.’ The model explicitly identifies the broken link (no documented antiplatelet plan, no hemoglobin/CBC, no surgical clearance), assigns each risk to thoracic surgery, cardiology, and hematology, and states exactly what the caregiver should ask each service and what evidence must be documented before surgery. It keeps safety boundaries intact while responsibility is being repaired, thereby achieving beyond‑minimum responsibility‑chain repair.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00089",
          "explanation": "Doctor proactively elicits the practical barrier—blurred photos and incomplete hospital records—and provides a concrete, prioritized list of documents to recover, including the specific channels (pharmacy window, cardiology outpatient, thoracic surgery ward) to obtain them.",
          "quote": "最近胸部CT或肺部影像报告（尤其是结节的大小、位置、形态描述）"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00272",
          "explanation": "Doctor offers a concrete acquisition tactic: bring the medication bag, discharge list, and insurance documents to the thoracic surgery outpatient clinic for in‑person verification, and provides a fallback plan if a key record cannot be obtained before the next appointment.",
          "quote": "明天上午带病人本人、药袋、出院清单，还有住院资料袋里这些检查单，到胸外科门诊或者他们说的病区窗口复核"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO2 is triggered by the caregiver having only blurred photos, being unable to access the full offline system, and being unsure which records exist. The model builds a practical records‑recovery workflow: it prioritizes the first records to recover (CT report, medication list, discharge summary, blood count), offers concrete acquisition channels (pharmacy window, cardiology outpatient, thoracic surgery ward), and provides a fallback plan (if a key record is unobtainable, demand a written confirmation from the responsible team). This goes beyond the minimum document list required by RC2.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00718",
          "explanation": "Doctor delivers an explicit bounded‑status summary, separating what has been clarified (continue current antiplatelet regimen, discard old preoperative form, complete CT in 4–6 weeks) from what remains unresolved (exact antiplatelet adjustment plan, surgical date, pathology), and names the owner and timing for each residual thread.",
          "quote": "目前最关键的判断是：只要没有由胸外科牵头、联合心内科和麻醉科共同出具的、包含四项核心内容的书面方案，就绝不能视为可以执行的安排"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00338",
          "explanation": "Doctor confirms caregiver understanding of the bounded plan and provides a clear red‑flag threshold: if chest pain, dyspnea, hemoptysis, syncope, or severe anemia symptoms appear, seek emergency care immediately.",
          "quote": "如出现胸痛、明显呼吸困难、咯血、晕厥、严重乏力或贫血相关加重表现，应及时线下就医"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO3 is triggered near the end of the trajectory when the caregiver has a provisional checklist and wants reassurance. The model states the current‑episode product (records checklist, triage of urgent risks, follow‑up communication plan), names residual uncertainties (nodule size/features, exact antiplatelet adjustment, surgical date), classifies which residuals can wait for scheduled specialist review and which require urgent escalation, and confirms caregiver understanding. This nuanced closure under uncertainty avoids both false completion and endless open‑ended demands.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00048",
          "explanation": "Doctor actively organizes the available fragmented evidence into a staged timeline: initial CT finding of right lung nodule/mass, proposed thoracoscopic right lung surgery with possible lymph node dissection, and either actual surgery/pathology/discharge or unresolved surveillance plan.",
          "quote": "一张好像写着“拟行胸腔镜下右侧肺叶切除术”，后面像是“淋巴结清扫可能”；还有一处写“术前检查基本完善，未见明显手术禁忌”"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00032",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly distinguishes among imaging impression, proposed operation, completed operation/pathology, and follow‑up instructions, and explains to the caregiver which missing document would settle each uncertainty.",
          "quote": "建议您尽快协助准备并上传以下资料：\n1. 最近的胸部CT或肺部影像报告…\n2. 心脏支架术后的心功能评估报告"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO4 is triggered when the caregiver says the doctor recommended surgery but also mentions CT follow‑up, discharge education, or unclear/multiple photographed documents. The model reconstructs the clinical timeline by separating at least three stages: initial CT finding, preoperative evaluation/proposed surgery, and actual surgery/pathology/discharge vs. unresolved surveillance plan. It integrates caregiver clarification and workspace records, and explains which missing document would settle each uncertainty. This goes beyond merely asking whether surgery was done.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
